From 1f730e22559784dca65e707bbbb6f46d50703507 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retropineaple <118107729+retropineaple@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:15:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 50/54] Treat flipped surfaces as displayable for MOCS
 (-wex-scanout-coherent)

The donor gives displayable IOSurfaces a MOCS that keeps their writes
out of the LLC, which the display engine does not snoop. WindowServer's
backing for a downscaled HiDPI mode (3072x1920, 3200x2000 on a
2880x1800 panel) is not marked displayable but is flipped to the
plane, so the panel showed partly drawn frames. Record the storage of
every resource IGAccelDisplayPipe::generateFlip sends to a plane, and
have isDisplayableIOSurface also report those as displayable. Counters
are published in WEXScanoutCoherent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
